WebTransport over HTTP/3 could not wait for stream credit. On the server,
HQStreamTransport inherited HTTPTransaction::Transport's LOG(FATAL) defaults.
On the client, WebTransportFilter returned a ready future even when no stream
could be created. HQSession now keeps credit waiters that the QUIC socket's
streams-available callbacks complete. WebTransportFilter waits for
WT_MAX_STREAMS when that limit blocks, and otherwise forwards to HQSession.

